                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Drone Zero Gravity is a game in which you guide a drone through various level with tons of obstacles, lasers, etc. The goal of the game is to get to the end of the level and find Data Orbs.\n\nThe music of Drone Zero Gravity is great in my opinion, a fitting space-type soundtrack that makes a great atmosphere to the game, I love it! The graphics are alright and the controls are fine. The stop button is a great tool for lasers and other obstacles, the pull/push mechanic is interesting and overall I think it's quite enjoyable to play.\n\nI don't know how long the game is, but it took me about 1 hour to pass the first 3 levels, the game is quite hard. I haven't reached the first Data Orb yet and there are 25 to collect, so I expect the game to be quite long. If you're looking for a somewhat challenging game, you should pick this up. It plays a bit like Unmechanical and they are both great games. :)",
